   Delta-compatible with v1 + Sprint 4 hardening checks. #}

## Dependency Table (11 Rules)

| # | From | To | Allowed? | Rule ID |
|---|------|----|----------|---------|
| R1 | Trust Foundation | Anything above | FORBIDDEN | DEP.trust_no_upward |
| R2 | Horizontal | Trust Foundation | Yes | DEP.h_reads_trust |
| R3 | Horizontal | Horizontal | Yes, cautiously | DEP.h_to_h_careful |
| R4 | Horizontal | Vertical | FORBIDDEN | DEP.h_no_vertical |
| R5 | Vertical | Trust Foundation | Yes | DEP.v_reads_trust |
| R6 | Vertical | Horizontal | Yes | DEP.v_uses_h |
| R7 | Vertical | Vertical | FORBIDDEN | DEP.v_no_v |
| R8 | Orchestration | Trust Foundation | Yes | DEP.orch_reads_trust |
| R9 | Orchestration | Horizontal | Yes | DEP.orch_uses_h |
| R10 | Orchestration | Vertical | Yes | DEP.orch_calls_v |
| R11 | Any | Orchestration | FORBIDDEN | DEP.no_upward_to_orch |

## Trust Foundation Rules

- **T1**: `trust/` has zero outward dependencies.
- **T2**: `trust/` remains pure (no I/O, no logging, no network).
- **T3**: shared trust models stay immutable (`ConfigDict(frozen=True)` where applicable).
- **T4**: signed vs unsigned metadata boundary is respected.

## Prompt/Review Rules (v2 Rollout)

- **PR.VER.1**: v2 prompts must coexist with v1 prompts (non-breaking rollout).
- **PR.VER.2**: review runtime can select prompt bundle version explicitly (`v1` or `v2`).
- **PR.VER.3**: default prompt selection remains backward-compatible (`v1`) unless requested.

## Deep-Agent Hardening Rules (Sprint 4)

- **DEEP.DOCS.1**: architecture docs enumerate deep-agent state/tool/planning/delegation capabilities.
- **DEEP.DOCS.2**: event taxonomy includes deep-agent execution events for observability and explainability.
- **DEEP.CLEAN.1**: no runtime imports from `deep_agents_from_scratch`.
- **DEEP.CLEAN.2**: cleanup is protected by architecture tests.

## Anti-Patterns

- **AP2**: vertical-to-vertical imports.
- **AP3**: hardcoded prompts.
- **AP6**: trust/shared types defined in service modules.
- **AP7**: horizontal trust service coupling.
- **AP8**: governance importing orchestration.
- **AP10**: lingering `deep_agents_from_scratch` references in runtime paths.
